- pbz2-core/src/randomized.rs: the table of numbers bzip2 uses for randomized
  blocks.
- testdata/sample1.bz2, sample2.bz2, sample3.bz2 and their .ref files: the
  sample files that ship with bzip2.
- testdata/randomized-blocks.bin and testdata/issue_137.bin: from the
  libbzip2-rs test suite.
- The tests in pbz2/tests/samples.rs follow the decompression tests of
  libbzip2-rs (https://github.com/trifectatechfoundation/libbzip2-rs) and
  bzip2-rs (https://github.com/paolobarbolini/bzip2-rs, MIT or Apache-2.0).
- The tests in pbz2/tests/compress.rs follow the compression tests of
  libbzip2-rs and of the bzip2 crate
  (https://github.com/trifectatechfoundation/bzip2-rs, MIT or Apache-2.0).

The suffix sort in pbz2-core/src/divsufsort/ is a Rust translation of
libdivsufsort 2.0 by Yuta Mori (https://github.com/y-256/libdivsufsort), under
the MIT license below. pbz2 changed it to write the Burrows-Wheeler column
straight into packed words and to report the row of a given suffix.

